WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.893
Here is a concrete maturity statement.

2
00:00:02.893 --> 00:00:13.093
The April twenty-third, twenty twenty-five release is explicitly a CV32A60X configuration release for technology readiness level five.

3
00:00:13.093 --> 00:00:23.445
Its scope includes an OBI interface, no caches, no physical memory protection entries, and a disabled instruction-fetch fence extension.

4
00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:28.089
The release also describes improvements to coverage and lint.

5
00:00:28.089 --> 00:00:31.819
Preserve that whole scope when citing the result.

6
00:00:31.819 --> 00:00:37.832
The package comparison earlier in this course uses a different source snapshot.

7
00:00:37.832 --> 00:00:45.749
The same configuration name on another branch does not automatically carry the release evidence forward.

8
00:00:45.749 --> 00:00:51.839
If you add features or change integration, identify what must be verified again.

9
00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:57.700
Safety certification is a separate assessment with its own required evidence.

